Standards Covered:
15.2 W3C Standards (HTML, CSS, JavaScript standards)
15.3 Accessibility (ADA compliance in forms)
15.4 Responsive Design (Bootstrap framework implementation)
15.6 GUI Objects (form inputs, buttons, dropdowns)
15.11 CSS and JS Frameworks (Bootstrap implementation)
Learning Objectives:
Create responsive forms using Bootstrap's grid system and form components
Implement accessible form elements following ADA compliance guidelines
Apply Bootstrap form validation classes and styling
Design mobile-first responsive forms that adapt to different screen sizes
Key Vocabulary:
Bootstrap Grid System
Form Validation States
Input Groups
Form Controls
Responsive Breakpoints
Accessibility Labels
ARIA Attributes
Daily Breakdown:
Day 1: Bootstrap Form Components
Bellwork: "What makes a form user-friendly on both desktop and mobile?"
Activity 1: Bootstrap CDN setup and grid system review (15 min)
Activity 2: Creating basic form structure with Bootstrap classes (20 min)
Activity 3: Implementing input groups, labels, and help text (15 min)
Closure: Quick form component identification quiz
Day 2: Responsive Design & Accessibility
Bellwork: "What challenges do users with disabilities face when filling out online forms?"
